  "id": "wave-of-excitation",
  "term": "wave of excitation",
  "definition": "In this historical account, a wave of excitation is the spread of nervous activity from one brain centre to others after a stimulus. As it moves outward, more centres take part, so conscious experience is understood as changing with the overall balance of cortical activity rather than coming from one isolated spot alone.",
